  "question": {
    "text": "The point of inflexion for the curve $y=(x-a)^n$, where n is odd integer and $n \\geq 3$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sdIjQ",
      "text": "$(a, 0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tpndW",
      "text": "$(0, a)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fqsYG",
      "text": "$(0,0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qehYt",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here $\\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}=n(n-1)(x-a)^{n-2}$\nNow, $\\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}=0 \\Rightarrow x=a$\nDifferentiating equation of the curve $n$ times,\nwe get, $\\frac{d^n y}{d x^n}=n$ !\n$\\therefore \\quad$ at $x=a, \\frac{d^n y}{d x^n} \\neq 0$ and $\\frac{d^{n-1} y}{d x^{n-1}}=0$,\nwhere $n$ is odd.\nTherefore $(a, 0)$ is the point of inflexion",
    "image": null
  },
